From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] oleacc: IAccPropServices property store

Every IAccPropServices method past QueryInterface returned E_NOTIMPL. Now a
process-wide store keyed by the identity string: SetPropValue, SetHwndProp,
SetHmenuProp (and the Str variants) keep a VARIANT; SetPropServer,
SetHwndPropServer, SetHmenuPropServer keep (and AddRef) the IAccPropServer;
ClearProps, ClearHwndProps, ClearHmenuProps drop and release them; setting
the same identity and property again releases the previous registration.
Compose/Decompose Hwnd/Hmenu identity strings round-trip through a tagged
struct (an hwnd string is rejected by the hmenu decomposer). Nothing reads
the store back into IAccessible queries yet (stated in the file comment).

Gate: test/accprop-gate.sh (test/accprop-probe.c).
Mutant SG_MUTANT_ACCPROP_NO_RELEASE_OLD (oleacc/propservice.c).
---
